\f1\fs22 Hayley took the equally well-appointed suite across the hall. Before closing her door, she paused in the hallway, catching Sarah\'92s eye. \'93I\'92ll work out how we leave,\'94 she said quietly. \'93When you\'92re ready.\'94 Hayley had spent years staking out secure buildings\'97who arrived when, which doors were used, where the gaps in attention strayed, covertly entering and leaving them by any means, if necessary. Sublime Point would be no different. \
In Sarah\'92s room, Kathy bounced on the side of the bed nearest the door. From her bag, she retrieved two patches and offered one to Sarah. Sarah waved it away as she fell like an audience volunteer at a hypnosis show, back-first on the bed alongside Kathy.\
