\f1\fs22 Sarah slept in fits and starts, cycling through dreams and nightmares. In the most traumatic of them, she was marrying a man dressed in a burger clown\'92s outfit, greasepaint thick on his face. She knew it must be Alexander beneath the costume, but the harder she tried to see his features, the more they morphed and blurred\'97from his mother\'92s calculating eyes, to Tony\'92s nervous grin, to painted-on features that smiled without meaning anything at all.\
